{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>You have renounced</b> — You have destroyed, as in: 'the renunciation of His sanctuary' (Lamentations 2:7). The nun is a root letter, and the zayin goes at the beginning, therefore לארץ."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {0 "The pun on נאר/הנזר (rearranging the same letters) is rendered literally; Ibn Ezra argues the root is נזר, with nun as first root letter."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:38.801573938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}